<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18009" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fervĕ-făcĭo</span></b> ,
			fēci, factum, 3 (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>in tmesi</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">postea ferve bene facito,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 157, 9</span></i>
			), v. a.
			ferveo + facio, <i>to cause to boil</i>,
				<i>to make hot</i>, <i>to heat</i>,
				<i>boil</i>, <i>melt</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eodem addito et oleum, postea fervefacito,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 156, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">muriam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					4, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patinae sese fervefaciunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 3, 2, 44</span></i>
			.—In <i>part. perf.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pix fervefacta,</span>”
				<i>melted pitch</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					G. 7</span></i>
			. 22 <i>fin.</i>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fervefacta jacula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 43, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					20, 3, 8, § 16</span></i>
			.</div>
